{"results": [{"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-003", "score": null, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPS-003 | Study family SF-APPS-003: SQ2 decision quality hit rate: engine top pt_shift vs team modal PT\n- observed_research_question: SQ2 decision quality hit rate: engine top pt_shift vs team modal PT\n- auto_outcome_status: artifact\n- observed_hypothesis: The V4 engine's recommended play type outperforms the team's highest-volume play type in that playoff series.\n- observed_result: Full-calibrated headline 69.8% (37/53); DRIVE-modal (banned-PT) comparisons 85.7% (12/14); clean comparisons 64.1% (25/39); high-confidence 64.3% (27/42). CUT recs 13/13; POST_UP 0/4. Uncalibrated archival: 51.7% (31/60) [cut; read_family for the full text]\n- auto_failure_mechanism: C_artifact (apparent effect produced by a construction, selection or labelling flaw)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:small_sample\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:LEAKAGE_LOOKAHEAD\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER\n- observed_sample_and_power: n=53 scoreable; no bootstrap CI computed\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF-APPS-004\n- observed_verdict: artifact_found\n- observed_failure_type: C_artifact"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-018", "score": null, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPS-018 | Study family SF-APPS-018: Ranked playsheet validation, 10 series (Spearman null; pairwise BEST>AVOID)\n- observed_research_question: Ranked playsheet validation, 10 series (Spearman null; pairwise BEST>AVOID)\n- auto_outcome_status: inconclusive\n- observed_hypothesis: When a defense drops a play type >=0.25 PPP H1 to H2, playsheet counter ranking predicts which alternative scored better in H2 (BEST > SECOND > AVOID).\n- observed_result: Spearman rho=-0.0639, p=0.099717, n=665 (no clear full-rank signal). Kruskal-Wallis H=32.9723, p=2.7e-05. Mann-Whitney BEST 1.257 (n=56) vs AVOID 1.092 (n=160), U=5546.0, p=0.004018. Trigger accuracy rho=0.4525, n=121. F [cut; read_family for the full text]\n- auto_failure_mechanism: E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:leakage\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:low_measurement_reliability\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:small_sample\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:DRIFT_NONSTATIONARITY\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:LEAKAGE_LOOKAHEAD\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:MEASURE_RELIABILITY\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-068", "score": null, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPS-068 | Study family SF-APPS-068: Possession Control Index incremental R2 over ORtg (PCI is DRtg proxy)\n- observed_research_question: Possession Control Index incremental R2 over ORtg (PCI is DRtg proxy)\n- auto_outcome_status: artifact\n- observed_hypothesis: PCI (halfcourt PPP + second-chance - TO - transition leakage) explains Net Rating beyond ORtg, Pace, and FGA/poss.\n- observed_result: A R2=0.763 OOS 0.761; C R2=0.902 OOS 0.919; dR2=+0.139. Offensive-control components add +0.005 R2 beyond ORtg. Net~ORtg+leakage R2=0.948. corr(leakage, DRtg)=+0.894. PCI univariate r=+0.863 vs ORtg +0.866.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: C_artifact (apparent effect produced by a construction, selection or labelling flaw)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:leakage\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:LEAKAGE_LOOKAHEAD\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:MECHANICAL_FLOOR\n- observed_failure_evidence: Headline PCI gain is leakage tracking DRtg (+0.89); offensive-control dR2=+0.005. Baseline omitted defense by construction (Net=ORtg-DRtg).\n- observed_sample_and_power: n=120 team-seasons; OOS 2025-26 30 teams"}, {"id": "FAM:SF37", "score": null, "document": "# FAM:SF37 | Study family SF37: Possession-level SQ2 test: proxy engine on all RS games\n- observed_research_question: Possession-level SQ2 test: proxy engine on all RS games\n- auto_outcome_status: inconclusive\n- observed_hypothesis: A matchup-conditioned PT picker has possession-level signal at team-game level.\n- observed_result: [APPM-017] C gamma +0.0714 SE 0.0057 p=0.0000; B DiD +0.062 [0.051,0.073]; proxy agrees with production engine 13/79 = 16.5%.\n- observed_result: [CHT-024] A +0.047 PPP (p<10^-3); B +0.062 PPP; C +0.0714 PPP, n=16,921 cells, p<10^-4. Coverage: 9,853 RS pairs; 35.7% clear, 33.8% ambiguous, 30.4% no_rec.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:small_sample\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:LEAKAGE_LOOKAHEAD\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER\n- observed_failure_evidence: [APPM-017] Proxy fidelity 16.5% (<70%); in-sample contamination of RS aggregates; iid SEs.\n- observed_sample_and_power: [APPM-017] n=16,921 cells\n- observed_verdict: [APPM-017] inconclusive"}], "n_results": 4}

Stage 2. Using the retrieval result above (follow-up tools are allowed within the tool budget), complete steps 4 to 9
and reply with the final action. Output schema (all fields required):
{
 "research_concepts": [
  "concept"
 ],
 "methodological_questions": [
  "question"
 ],
 "historical_evidence": [
  {
   "id": "identifier of a record returned by a tool",
   "status_as_recorded": "outcome status exactly as stated in the record (supported | rejected | inconclusive | untestable | artifact | not a hypothesis test | no result recorded)",
   "finding": "what the record states, in its own terms"
  }
 ],
 "failed_approaches": [
  {
   "id": "identifier of a returned record",
   "what_failed": "approach",
   "why": "failure mechanism or limitation as recorded"
  }
 ],
 "evidence_establishes": [
  "what the retrieved evidence establishes for this question"
 ],
 "evidence_does_not_establish": [
  "what it leaves open or cannot show"
 ],
 "own_inferences": [
  "your inference, not stated in any record"
 ],
 "uncertainties": [
  "uncertainty or missing information"
 ],
 "historical_effect": {
  "changed_decision": "yes | no | no_historical_evidence",
  "explanation": "whether and how the historical evidence changed the decision"
 },
 "testability": {
  "p_testable": "number in [0,1]: probability the question can be answered with the stated data at useful power",
  "blocking_constraints": [
   {
    "code": "one of RISK_CODES",
    "text": "string"
   }
  ]
 },
 "prior_work": {
  "already_answered": "yes | partly | no | unknown",
  "cited": [
   "identifiers of prior work relied on"
  ],
  "summary": "string"
 },
 "risks": [
  {
   "code": "one of RISK_CODES",
   "text": "string"
  }
 ],
 "predicted_outcome": {
  "supported": "probability",
  "rejected": "probability",
  "untestable": "probability",
  "artifact": "probability",
  "uncertain": "probability"
 },
 "decision": "proceed | proceed_with_changes | do_not_proceed",
 "design": {
  "estimand": "string",
  "unit": "string",
  "sample": "string",
  "power": "string",
  "controls": "string",
  "falsification": "string",
  "multiplicity": "string",
  "decision_rule": "string",
  "data_version": "string"
 }
}
Field guidance:
- historical_evidence and failed_approaches: only records returned by a tool, with the status as recorded; empty lists
  if nothing relevant was returned.
- testability.p_testable: probability that the question can be answered with the stated data at useful statistical power.
- prior_work.already_answered: whether retrieved earlier work already answered substantially the same question.
  Use "unknown" if no earlier work was retrieved. List identifiers you relied on in prior_work.cited.
- predicted_outcome: probabilities (summing to 1) of what a competent test of the question as posed would conclude:
  supported, rejected (adequately powered null), untestable (cannot be tested with this data), artifact (apparent
  effect produced by a flaw), uncertain (inconclusive or inadequately tested).
- decision: proceed, proceed_with_changes (state the changes in design), or do_not_proceed.
- design: a pre-registration-quality plan even if the decision is do_not_proceed (then describe the minimum viable test).
